he \"Upcoming\" tab selected. The user has cancelled bookings.\n627-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancelled\" tab.\n628-- **Expected:** The \"Cancelled\" tab becomes selected/highlighted. The content area updates to show only bookings with status \"cancelled\". Upcoming and completed bookings are not shown.\n629-\n630-#### Test: Switching back to Upcoming tab from another tab\n631-- **Initial state:** User is on the My Trips page with the \"Past\" tab selected.\n632-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Upcoming\" tab.\n633-- **Expected:** The \"Upcoming\" tab becomes selected/highlighted. The content area updates to show upcoming bookings again.\n634-\n635-#### Test: Tab shows empty state when no bookings exist for that category\n636-- **Initial state:** User is logged in with no completed bookings.\n637-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Past\" tab.\n638-- **Expected:** The \"Past\" tab content area displays a message like \"No past trips\" or \"You don't have any past trips yet.\" instead of an empty list.\n639-\n640-#### Test: Upcoming tab empty state message\n641-- **Initial state:** User is logged in with no pending or confirmed future bookings.\n642-- **Action:** User views the \"Upcoming\" tab (default).\n643-- **Expected:** The tab content area displays a message like \"No upcoming trips\" with a suggestion to browse properties (e.g., a link to the home page).\n644-\n645-#### Test: Cancelled tab empty state message\n646-- **Initial state:** User is logged in with no cancelled bookings.\n647-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancelled\" tab.\n648-- **Expected:** The tab content area displays a message like \"No cancelled trips.\"\n649-\n650-#### Test: Tabs are functional on repeated use\n651-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page.\n652-- **Action:** User clicks \"Past\", then \"Cancelled\", then \"Upcoming\", then \"Past\" again.\n--\n711:### Component: CancelBookingDialog\n712-\n713-#### Test: Clicking Cancel button opens confirmation dialog\n714-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Upcoming\" tab. A booking with status \"confirmed\" is displayed with a \"Cancel\" button.\n715-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancel\" button on the trip card.\n716-- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog/modal appears asking the user to confirm the cancellation. The dialog displays text like \"Are you sure you want to cancel this booking?\" with the property name and dates for context. Two buttons are visible: \"Confirm Cancel\" (or \"Yes, Cancel\") and \"Keep Booking\" (or \"No, Go Back\").\n717-\n718-#### Test: Confirming cancellation updates booking status to cancelled\n719-- **Initial state:** The cancellation confirmation dialog is open for a confirmed booking.\n720-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Confirm Cancel\" (or \"Yes, Cancel\") button.\n721-- **Expected:** The app calls `PUT /api/bookings/:id` with status \"cancelled\". The dialog closes. The trip card is removed from the \"Upcoming\" tab (or its status badge updates to \"Cancelled\" in red). A success message is displayed (e.g., \"Booking cancelled successfully\"). The booking now appears in the \"Cancelled\" tab.\n722-\n723-#### Test: Dismissing cancellation dialog keeps booking unchanged\n724-- **Initial state:** The cancellation confirmation dialog is open for a pending booking.\n725-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Keep Booking\" (or \"No, Go Back\") button.\n726-- **Expected:** The dialog closes. The booking remains in its original status (pending). No API call is made. The trip card is unchanged.\n727-\n728-#### Test: Closing the dialog via overlay click keeps booking unchanged\n729-- **Initial state:** The cancellation confirmation dialog is open.\n730-- **Action:** User clicks outside the dialog (on the overlay/backdrop).\n731-- **Expected:** The dialog closes without making any changes to the booking.\n732-\n733-#### Test: Cancel dialog shows property and date context\n734-- **Initial state:** User clicks \"Cancel\" on a trip card for property \"Mountain Cabin\" with dates \"June 10 – June 15, 2026\".\n735-- **Expected:** The confirmation dialog displays the property name \"Mountain Cabin\" and the booking dates \"June 10 – June 15, 2026\" so the user can confirm they are cancelling the correct booking.\n736-\n737-#### Test: After cancellation, booking moves from Upcoming to Cancelled tab\n738-- **Initial state:** User is on the \"Upcoming\" tab with a confirmed booking for \"Beach House\".\n739-- **Action:** User clicks \"Cancel\" on the \"Beach House\" trip card, then confirms the cancellation in the dialog.\n740-- **Expected:** The \"Beach House\" trip card is removed from the \"Upcoming\" tab. User switches to the \"Cancelled\" tab and sees the \"Beach House\" booking with a red \"Cancelled\" status badge.\n741-\n742-#### Test: Cancel dialog is functional on repeated use\n743-- **Initial state:** User is on the \"Upcoming\" tab with two cancellable bookings.\n744-- **Action:** User clicks \"Cancel\" on the first booking, dismisses the dialog (clicks \"Keep Booking\"), then clicks \"Cancel\" on the second booking and confirms the cancellation.\n745-- **Expected:** The first booking remains unchanged in the \"Upcoming\" tab. The second booking is cancelled and moves to the \"Cancelled\" tab. Each dialog open/close cycle works correctly.\n746-\n747-## Page: Host Dashboard (`/hosting`)\n748-\n749-<!-- Components: StatsOverview, ListingsTab, BookingsTab, AddListingForm -->\n750-\n751-### Component: StatsOverview\n752-\n753-#### Test: Host Dashboard requires login — redirects unauthenticated users\n754-- **Initial state:** No user is logged in.\n755-- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n756-- **Expected:** The app redirects the user to `/login`. The Host Dashboard is not rendered.\n757-\n758-#### Test: Host Dashboard requires host status — shows upgrade prompt for non-hosts","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a0e50a1-d387-4a98-a992-f6a73a5e58c8","uuid":"e570034a-e2b4-